    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "citations = [3, 0, 6, 1, 5]  ->  3   (3 papers with at least 3 citations)\ncitations = [1, 3, 1]        ->  1\ncitations = [10, 8, 9]       ->  3   (h can't exceed the number of papers)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The idea: sorted, the h-th best paper decides"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Sort the citations from most to least cited. Then \"h papers with at least h citations\" means: the first h papers all have at least h — and since they're sorted, only the **weakest of them**, the h-th, needs checking. So walk down the sorted list while paper number `h + 1` still has at least `h + 1` citations. Where that fails, h is the answer."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "1. Brute force: try every h"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function hIndex(citations) {\n  for (let h = citations.length; h > 0; h--) {\n    const enough = citations.filter((c) => c >= h).length;   // papers with at least h citations\n    if (enough >= h) return h;\n  }\n  return 0;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def h_index(citations):\n    for h in range(len(citations), 0, -1):\n        if sum(1 for c in citations if c >= h) >= h:   # papers with at least h citations\n            return h\n    return 0"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "int hIndex(int[] citations) {\n    for (int h = citations.length; h > 0; h--) {\n        int enough = 0;\n        for (int c : citations) if (c >= h) enough++;   // papers with at least h citations\n        if (enough >= h) return h;\n    }\n    return 0;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "int hIndex(vector<int>& citations) {\n    for (int h = citations.size(); h > 0; h--) {\n        int enough = 0;\n        for (int c : citations) if (c >= h) enough++;   // papers with at least h citations\n        if (enough >= h) return h;\n    }\n    return 0;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n²), space O(1).** Up to n candidate values of h, each counted over all n papers."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "2. Sort descending, then count"
    },
    {
      "type": "simulator",
      "program": "h-index",
      "caption": "Sorted most cited first, h grows while paper #(h+1) still has at least h+1 citations."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function hIndex(citations) {\n  const c = [...citations].sort((a, b) => b - a);   // most cited first\n  let h = 0;\n  while (h < c.length && c[h] >= h + 1) h++;        // the (h+1)-th best paper has at least h+1 citations\n  return h;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def h_index(citations):\n    c = sorted(citations, reverse=True)   # most cited first\n    h = 0\n    while h < len(c) and c[h] >= h + 1:   # the (h+1)-th best paper has at least h+1 citations\n        h += 1\n    return h"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "int hIndex(int[] citations) {\n    int[] c = citations.clone();\n    Arrays.sort(c);                                   // ascending: read it from the end\n    int n = c.length, h = 0;\n    while (h < n && c[n - 1 - h] >= h + 1) h++;       // the (h+1)-th best paper has at least h+1 citations\n    return h;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "int hIndex(vector<int>& citations) {\n    vector<int> c = citations;\n    sort(c.begin(), c.end(), greater<int>());         // most cited first\n    int h = 0;\n    while (h < (int)c.size() && c[h] >= h + 1) h++;   // the (h+1)-th best paper has at least h+1 citations\n    return h;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n log n), space O(n)** for the sorted copy."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "3. Counting: no sort needed"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "h can never exceed n, so any paper with more than n citations can be counted as n. Count how many papers have each number of citations from 0 to n, then walk down from n adding up papers until the total reaches the current value."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function hIndex(citations) {\n  const n = citations.length;\n  const count = new Array(n + 1).fill(0);\n  for (const c of citations) count[Math.min(c, n)]++;   // more than n citations counts as n\n  let papers = 0;\n  for (let h = n; h > 0; h--) {\n    papers += count[h];                                 // papers with at least h citations\n    if (papers >= h) return h;\n  }\n  return 0;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def h_index(citations):\n    n = len(citations)\n    count = [0] * (n + 1)\n    for c in citations:\n        count[min(c, n)] += 1             # more than n citations counts as n\n    papers = 0\n    for h in range(n, 0, -1):\n        papers += count[h]                # papers with at least h citations\n        if papers >= h:\n            return h\n    return 0"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "int hIndex(int[] citations) {\n    int n = citations.length;\n    int[] count = new int[n + 1];\n    for (int c : citations) count[Math.min(c, n)]++;   // more than n citations counts as n\n    int papers = 0;\n    for (int h = n; h > 0; h--) {\n        papers += count[h];                            // papers with at least h citations\n        if (papers >= h) return h;\n    }\n    return 0;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "int hIndex(vector<int>& citations) {\n    int n = citations.size();\n    vector<int> count(n + 1, 0);\n    for (int c : citations) count[min(c, n)]++;        // more than n citations counts as n\n    int papers = 0;\n    for (int h = n; h > 0; h--) {\n        papers += count[h];                            // papers with at least h citations\n        if (papers >= h) return h;\n    }\n    return 0;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n), space O(n).** A counting sort in disguise — the key insight is capping at n."
    },
